Flora:

Thorned Starvines: Genetically aggressive vine species that compete with human crops and regenerate from cuttings. Dangerous in monsoon season.

Cradle Moss: Absorbs ambient toxins and releases spore clouds once per year; used in air purification and biofilter tech.

Fauna:

Gleamshrews: Semi-sapient rodent species with iridescent fur; considered a pest but have potential for biotech data storage (being studied).

Sister Wasps: Symbiotic wasps introduced by early biotech firms to control insect populations. Swarm dangerously if hives are disrupted.
